      ]
    },
    "offer_browser_tts": "true",
    "teacher_markdown": "**Intent:** AI as ideation partner, not just code generator. When a student has a feeling (\"dark and mysterious\") but no concrete design, the strong move is to ask for options in words first, then choose. This keeps the student in the director's chair. The AI is configured to describe options without changing anything until the student picks one.\r\n\r\n**Circulation questions:**\r\n\r\n- \"What three directions did AI offer? Which did you pick, and why?\"\r\n- \"How is asking for ideas different from asking for a change?\"\r\n\r\n**Expected mistakes and misconceptions:**\r\n\r\n- Students may skip straight to \"make it dark and mysterious\" - that works, but ask them what they gave up (the choice between directions)\r\n- Students may treat AI's first idea as the only answer - remind them they can ask for three more\r\n",
    "require_edit_to_continue": "true"
  },
